  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Infrastructure for the future (f. Project Science)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The EBRD has signed a sovereign loan of up to EUR 80 million in favour of the  Republic of Serbia for the construction and expansion of modern science and  technology parks (&quot;STPs&quot;) in Serbia.  The Bank&apos;s first committed tranche of EUR 70 million will be used to finance  the construction, fit-out and the purchase of new equipment for the expansion  of existing and development of new STP facilities in the cities of Ni&#x161;, Cacak,  and Kru&#x161;evac, to support critical infrastructure for the incubation and growth  of innovative start-ups and businesses in Serbia. The Bank&apos;s second committed  tranche of EUR 10 million will be used for the development of STP facilities  within the new biotechnology park Bio4 or for further expansion of STPs in  Belgrade and Novi Sad, subject to the Government of Serbia&apos;s (&quot;GoS&quot;) priorities  and timeline.</narrative>
  </description>
